<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">throttle</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">throttle</ansi> command drives your natural fangs into your
opponent's throat in a crushing choke, cutting off their air.
It deals direct damage, applies a lingering stamina drain, and
tests whether their concentration can survive the grip if they
are casting a spell.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must have natural fangs (fanged species only)
  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">throttle</ansi>
  Attempt to throttle your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Moderate. The choke bite deals direct harm.
  <ansi fg="stat">Bleed:</ansi> A successful throttle opens shallow throat wounds
    that bleed briefly.
  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina Drain:</ansi> The Throttled condition saps stamina over
    several rounds as the victim struggles for breath.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cast Interrupt:</ansi> When the victim is casting a spell, the
    choke tests their grip on it. Their own Willpower and
    spellcasting training contest the throttle, so a practiced
    caster can hold through it, while a novice is more likely to
    lose the spell entirely. When it breaks, their unspent
    conviction is partially refunded but the spell is lost.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with other special moves.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Throttle spends Stamina and requires full payment before the bite. Carried load
raises the price, while <ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi> skill lowers it.
If you are too spent, no cooldown, combat round, or effect is consumed.

Throttle rewards patience and is most valuable when an opponent is
mid-incantation, letting you silence the spell before it fires.

